        yield item
```

Strings aren't Iterators anyway (str has no __next__), but bytes? bytes also has no __next__. The test has b'fghj' expected to stay as-is — bytes is not an Iterator so fine. But nested: item could be an iterator at nested level, e.g. file object inside the list. Recursing into expand_list_generator(item) iterates it fine since top-level loop iterates any iterable.

